WEBVTT

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.240
High Commander Fudo is gone?

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.860
He left a note.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.240
It seems that he left early this morning.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:23.630
To search for... the Legendary Aquarion?

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:25.830
Does he have a lead on it?

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.820
I don't know.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.200
There may be something in the Book of Twin Stars, but...

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.820
The Book of Twin Stars?

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.360
Why are there so many holes?

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.940
He's in this one!

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.380
Not again. This one's really deep.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.420
Andy!

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.540
What's the matter with him?

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.420
Why is he so depressed after he saved all of us?

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.710
Andy dug us an awesome hot spring!

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.120
What happened out there?

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.060
Mix, do you have any idea?

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.840
Nope! No idea!

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.840
What possibly could have happened?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.600
Oh, no!

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.980
Mix...

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.030
A concert?

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.960
Thank you. I'll think about it.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.220
Don't think about it. Come with me.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:11.530
I'll be waiting.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:12.290
Later!

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.720
You got asked out again?

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.550
Your new look's doing wonders for you, Zessica.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.930
It's not sweet enough.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:28.100
And how about your daring confession in the mock battle?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.060
You were so brave!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.640
Sorry, did I make you do that?

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.070
Not really. I said it because I wanted to.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.360
Besides, it helped me move forward.

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:43.570
Really?

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:49.400
But I might be moving towards another dead end...

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:53.920
Miss Suzushiro!

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.020
Yes?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.210
Perfect. I was going to take this up to your room.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.760
Here you go.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.920
Thank you.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.140
Mikono!

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:12.390
Oh, I'm sorry. I wasn't trying to hide this.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.900
It's a letter from my father.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:16.040
Your father?

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.200
We don't really get along.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.680
I wasn't expecting a letter from him.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.840
Maybe he's worried about me.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.520
Well, of course. He's your dad.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.800
I guess I'm not one to talk.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.040
Oh, no...

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.940
I remember my mom a little bit,

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:40.060
but nothing about my dad.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.680
I don't even know what's going on right now.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.310
You mean...

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:52.810
why I protected him?

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.520
Stop!

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.060
Don't shoot, Amata!

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.650
Please forgive him!

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:03.190
I don't mean to blame you for anything!

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:06.570
But we all have to work together now.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.620
I know!

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:13.290
I'm the one who's supposed to connect everyone together.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:16.670
But I don't know if I can!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.960
Mikono!

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.410
This isn't...

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:45.400
Well, this is different. What's the matter?

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:49.370
Father sent you a letter, and it got delivered to me by mistake.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:52.870
Sorry. I opened it already.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.980
Yeah, Dad's handwriting is terrible.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.650
And why'd he send a sealed letter, anyway?

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:00.670
Hey, what's wrong?

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:02.900
Nothing.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.640
See you tomorrow.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.420
Mikono!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.700
<i>I'm so stupid.</i>

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.640
<i>I shouldn't have kept reading it.</i>

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:23.290
<i>I don't know why Mikono is at the academy,</i>

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:27.190
<i>but I hope she isn't holding you back.</i>

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:32.460
<i>You know that she's never been good at anything.</i>

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.880
<i>Just say the word and I'll have her out of Neo-Deava</i>

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.580
<i>and back home with me.</i>

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:46.670
<i>I'm still completely useless to Daddy.</i>

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:47.640
Mikono?

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.180
You're worried about Andy?

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:58.780
He's really depressed right now.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.800
And it's all my fault.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.220
But I thought you two were getting along really well.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:08.190
A few things happened on that field trip.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:13.440
The worst part is that I go around telling people to say what they feel,

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:17.420
but when the time came, I just couldn't do it.

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:21.960
I can't stop seeing my dad in boys.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.850
Your dad?

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:28.120
You know why I have boy problems, right?

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.000
Yeah...

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.940
How about you, Mikono?

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:33.580
How's your relationship with your dad?

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:35.970
Me? I...

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:40.230
Um...

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.100
What is it, Mikono?

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:47.110
If you're not going to tell me...

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:52.360
I was always afraid of what he thought of me.

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.760
Whenever I was about to say something,

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.820
I'd get scared that he'd be angry, and stop.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:01.840
But he'd get mad at me for not speaking my mind anyway.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.370
Oh.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:07.160
I guess we'll never understand.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:10.180
Dads are men, too, after all.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:14.890
And we girls can't figure out how men feel.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:23.550
By the way, is Shush a boy or a girl?

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:24.230
Well...

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:36.180
Zessica?

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:39.740
Why are you practicing at this hour?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.960
I remembered that I'm a fighter.

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.720
I know I've been depressed lately,

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.840
but I don't want to lose the one edge I've got.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.400
Good night!

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:55.420
Zessica...

00:09:05.050 --> 00:09:07.190
What am I doing?

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.450
This is a dead end.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:25.240
Ianthe's operating level has just passed 40%.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:29.760
The amount of energy required for dimensional warping is what's hurting us the most.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:35.840
Continued travel to Vega will put a strain on the populace.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.470
Mass rebellions have been forecasted.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:43.060
Then we've reached the end of the line.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.320
Where is Kagura?

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.560
I'm sorry. We don't know.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:53.040
Mikage is probably behind this.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:58.320
He doesn't care one bit about Altair's future.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:03.800
Prepare the Ahura Gnis to sortie.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.020
Sir?

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.080
I'm going to Vega myself.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:15.400
It's time to taste the air of that old battlefield.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:27.000
Alicia...

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:31.290
For the sake of bringing this world back to life,

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.820
I shall find the True Eve.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.570
And I might also find...

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:43.700
the son you left on Vega.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.580
You read it, didn't you?

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.400
You know, Dad's letter.

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:55.780
I'm sorry.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:58.880
I don't really mind.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.120
I was just worried it was getting you down.

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:07.940
Parents freak out about the stupidest things.

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:12.100
You can send me home.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.240
What?

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:19.510
Daddy's right. I'm holding you guys back.

00:11:19.510 --> 00:11:23.260
If I'm going to be useless, I should do it at home.

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:24.620
Mikono!

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:27.000
Ow!

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:29.910
What was that for?

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.920
You've always been too worried about what people think of you.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:40.700
You could never say anything because you were
scared of making people mad or hurting them.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:44.800
But I think you were mostly scared for yourself.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:52.810
For a long time, I thought of you as my useless coward of a sister.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:57.820
But I met this guy, and right away, he said...

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.240
<i>I realize I haven't known her for very long,</i>

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.910
<i>but I think she's changed since then.</i>

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:11.160
Mikono's trying hard to change herself!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.800
Amata told you that?

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.940
As much as I hate to admit it, he was right.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.920
You've really changed.

00:12:21.330 --> 00:12:23.930
In fact, I want Dad to see how you've changed.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:26.500
Cayenne!

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:44.110
That's a new sound.

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:47.620
A powerful, intense sound.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:55.000
The sea. It's making me nostalgic.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:58.250
This is the Vega of my youth.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:03.660
Oh, Izumo. You want to bloom a flower after all this time?

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:09.760
Or are you looking for a seed dropped by a flower?

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:12.620
We've sighted an unknown enemy mech!

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.600
Looks like we have a boss battle coming up!

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:18.580
You're late, Andy!

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:19.480
Sorry...

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:27.500
Are you okay?

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:30.280
Sure. I'm fine...

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:37.670
Andy!

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.170
You can't dig in here!

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:44.170
Forget it. He's out of commission.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:49.040
We have five usable Vectors! Have two of them back up Aquarion!

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:50.600
The Elements going out are...

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.960
They're up to you.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.930
Cayenne! Amata! And...

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:56.680
I'll go!

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:00.060
You can't! It's too dangerous for you to go!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.940
I can't be myself if you won't let me fight!

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:07.200
Right now, we have to be fighters before girls!

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:09.950
We want to help and be part of the team!

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.030
What are you...

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.600
Let them go.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:17.460
We can only do so much with men alone.

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:22.590
Fudo... did I do the right thing?

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:26.380
Then Aquarion's pilots are Amata, Zessica, and Malloy!

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.090
Cayenne and Mix, you're the wingmen!

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:29.340
Roger!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:34.840
Zessica's too excited.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:37.180
I'm worried about her.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.780
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:48.070
Let's Unite! I'll be the head, got it?

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:49.480
Zessica...

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:50.070
Roger!

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:51.820
Heartbreak Union!

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:54.620
Go, Aquarion!

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:02.880
I can be with Amata, if only in a fight...

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.460
I can feel Zessica's emotions!

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:08.220
Union is amazing!

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:11.850
Aquarion Gepard!

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.600
We'll deal with the grunts!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:22.140
We may just be Vectors, but we'll still mess you up!

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:34.420
Let's end this!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.870
Good effort, but you're still greenhorns.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.160
No way!

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:45.130
He didn't take any damage at all!

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:58.430
Damage report!

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:01.480
West side barriers have been obliterated!

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:05.310
The enemy unit absorbed Gepard's beam, amplified it, and fired it back!

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.820
How about these?

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:14.860
Such youthful passion is lost on Altair.

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:17.280
But it won't win you this battle alone!

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:29.060
Calm down, Zessica!

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:30.710
It's too dangerous to shoot him!

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:32.740
Get in closer!

00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:34.550
I know already!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:40.180
Malloy! Back me up!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.390
Got it!

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.890
The Curse of Malloy!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.400
Contrary Twister!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:59.300
How's that feel?

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.570
Fragility? Interesting.

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:09.540
But the young are always more fragile than the old.

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:15.000
I would like to avoid needless destruction...

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:18.050
So let me demonstrate the vast gap between our powers.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.390
One more time! Contrary Twister!

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:23.430
That won't work again!

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:31.190
Gepard!

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.340
The Union broke!

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:38.860
That impact knocked Malloy out!

00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:41.120
Vector Y is flying on autopilot!

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:42.790
I'll go!

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.710
Element Change to Mikono!

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:47.460
Cayenne, Amata, and Mikono will Unite!

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.280
Zessica, back them up!

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.210
Why?

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:53.140
You're too hotheaded today!

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:54.600
What's the matter with you?

00:17:57.450 --> 00:18:00.280
Amata! Cayenne! We're going to Unite!

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.640
The enemy is heading this way!

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:10.650
That Abductor doesn't look like it's attacking...

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.360
He's tapping into our communications!

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.160
What?

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:21.320
Soldiers of Vega.

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:27.260
I am Izumo Kamurogi, chief commander of the planet Altair.

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:30.040
I would like to speak to your leader.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.360
The chief commander?

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:33.720
Him?

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:40.340
I am Crea Dolosera, the commander of Neo-Deava.

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:44.380
Even your commander is an Igura, a female.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:48.810
I was under the impression that
women were not disposed to battle.

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:51.260
Perhaps what you say is true.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:56.070
But when necessary, women can be even stronger than men.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.620
Perhaps.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:02.820
We require the most powerful Rare Igura among you.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:07.830
The most powerful Rare Igura?

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:13.300
I have no desire to wage war on this world.

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:18.340
All I ask is that you send a Rare Igura to our planet.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.620
No way in hell!

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:21.800
Wait.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.840
Miss Chairman?

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:28.060
If we have a chance to settle this diplomatically...

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:30.060
What would Fudo do?

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:35.520
Zessica's Vector is heading towards the Abductor!

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:41.140
You want a woman? Take me!

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:43.410
Maybe that'll change things!

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:47.080
That machine...

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:49.860
So it is a Rare Igura!

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:58.300
Cut it out, Zessica!

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:03.760
Don't throw yourself away! You're not thinking straight!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.680
Yes, I am! I...

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.860
I see that Rare Igura has a strong will.

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:10.680
I'll take her.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.650
Pursuit Union!

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.360
Go Aquarion!

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.030
Aquarion Evol!

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:26.580
The flying Machine Angel!

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:37.180
I sense... him inside the machine...

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:41.760
Let's make sure, Izumo.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:44.010
With your very own eyes.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:54.420
Mom?

00:20:54.990 --> 00:20:57.110
Why is that image there?

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:04.560
Something is manipulating Amata's heart.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:09.870
Clear, sweet, yet bitter.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:13.650
Mikage, you snake! This is your doing!

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:16.630
But it stopped the Machine Angel.

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:19.880
It really is him...

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:22.900
What's happening?

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.020
Amata! Stay focused on your enemy!

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:25.590
Zessica!

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.550
I won't let you take Zessica!

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.990
Don't regret this, Zessica!

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:47.410
Mix!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:57.220
I won't let you! Infinity Punch!

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:02.800
Let us meet again, winged boy.

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:15.680
She sacrificed herself for me...

00:22:16.030 --> 00:22:17.000
Mix...

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:40.040
Mix!

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.760
I hated myself for being afraid.

00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:17.500
But maybe fear is what gives us the power to move forward.

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:21.770
I have to take my own step forward.

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:25.110
Next time: First Reunion.
